# AlphaClone Dashboard Consistency

- Treat dashboard work as one product system, not one-off screens. New modules must match existing AlphaClone primitives before inventing new chrome.
- Reuse shared primitives first: `ModuleFrame`, `KpiCard`, `ModuleDashboardLayout`, `ModuleDashboardView`, `DashboardChartCard`, shared `Button`, `Badge`, `EmptyState`/`OsEmptyState`, and workspace panel classes from `src/constants/design.ts` / `brand.ts`.
- Do not introduce generic AI-SaaS defaults: no random `rounded-2xl/3xl`, heavy one-off shadows, gradient hero blocks, colorful icon chips on every stat, or ad hoc white-card layouts.
- Keep tokens synchronized. If you touch dashboard styling, update `src/constants/brand.ts`, `src/constants/design.ts`, and workspace CSS in `globals.css` together instead of hardcoding local values.
- Match one spacing/radius/elevation rhythm across modules. Prefer Alphaclone OS workspace/enterprise tokens; avoid literal sizes unless the token layer is being updated intentionally.
- Respect each module's real information shape. CRM should not look like invoicing just because both can be rendered as cards and tables.
- Module identity icons come from `@/components/icons/alphaclone`. Lucide is fine for generic affordances only.
- Empty, loading, and error states must explain what happened and what the user should do next. Never fail silently.
- Before finishing, compare against at least two existing modules and check: header anatomy, panel chrome, primary actions, table/list row behavior, status badges, and empty states.
